# — Agent Rules for Cursor & AI Assistants

Always follow the engineering guidelines defined in `AGENTS.md`.

## ZERO-WASTE CI GATE (PRE-PUSH VERIFICATION)
Do NOT push code to GitHub before completing and verifying all 3 local checks:
1. `pnpm check:type` (0 errors)
2. `pnpm run lint` (0 errors, all files formatted)
3. `pnpm run build:workstation` (11 packages build successfully)

## PNPM CATALOG RULE
- Dependencies added to `apps/workstation/package.json` MUST use `"catalog:"`.
- Versions must be defined in `pnpm-workspace.yaml` under `catalog:`.
- Never use direct version strings like `"0.2.1"` in package.json.
- Remove any unused catalog items to avoid `pnpm/yaml-no-unused-catalog-item`.

## CI MINUTES CONSERVATION
- Add `[skip ci]` or `[ci skip]` in commit messages for any docs, plans, scratch files, or non-code changes.
- Batch commits atomically before pushing. Never micro-push single-line edits.
- Use `gh run list` and `gh run cancel <id>` to cancel redundant or hanging CI runs immediately.
